1
00:01:25,170 --> 00:01:27,020
Read this poem.

2
00:01:27,220 --> 00:01:29,440
I could tell at a glance it was yours.

3
00:01:29,840 --> 00:01:31,450
Please forgive me.

4
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:33,759
I didn’t know my place.

5
00:01:35,410 --> 00:01:37,210
What do you think? Am I amazing?

6
00:01:37,210 --> 00:01:38,250
Who are you?

7
00:01:38,250 --> 00:01:40,020
You’re not my younger brother.

8
00:01:40,580 --> 00:01:41,940
Ah!

9
00:01:41,940 --> 00:01:42,720
My lord!

10
00:01:46,410 --> 00:01:48,880
I told you I'm a doctor.

11
00:02:05,470 --> 00:02:07,300
The Fool represents a new beginning.

12
00:02:08,479 --> 00:02:11,470
You’re about to start a new role and new relationships

13
00:02:13,170 --> 00:02:14,670
somewhere far, far away.

14
00:02:15,590 --> 00:02:18,430
Am I going to fall in love with a foreigner?

15
00:02:21,130 --> 00:02:22,740
That’s not what the card says.

16
00:02:22,740 --> 00:02:25,390
It says they’re from your country.

17
00:02:32,390 --> 00:02:35,530
You can hesitate, but don’t lie to yourself.

18
00:02:36,910 --> 00:02:39,120
Deep down, you know how you feel,

19
00:02:40,260 --> 00:02:43,160
but something make you afraid

20
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:44,240
or uncertain.

21
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:17,660
I wish I could bathe with you like this

22
00:03:18,329 --> 00:03:19,570
every day.

23
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:22,720
You can.

24
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:54,130
I’m sorry.

25
00:03:55,220 --> 00:03:56,510
It’s alright.

26
00:04:41,409 --> 00:04:43,250
We didn’t know each other.

27
00:04:44,370 --> 00:04:45,790
What happened back then

28
00:04:46,450 --> 00:04:48,330
wasn’t anyone’s fault.

29
00:04:51,790 --> 00:04:53,100
But this time,

30
00:04:54,820 --> 00:04:56,980
we both know

31
00:04:57,670 --> 00:05:00,450
that our duty is to remain loyal

32
00:05:00,930 --> 00:05:03,070
and faithful to the king.

33
00:05:04,340 --> 00:05:05,230
Isn’t that right?

34
00:05:08,780 --> 00:05:09,650
Yes.

35
00:05:28,280 --> 00:05:30,050
Can’t sleep again?

36
00:05:32,280 --> 00:05:33,620
You too?

37
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:40,370
Then come drink with me.

38
00:06:03,850 --> 00:06:05,640
The moon is beautiful.

39
00:06:16,630 --> 00:06:18,860
That’s why I wish it could stay forever.

40
00:06:22,930 --> 00:06:25,040
If the moonlight were to disappear,

41
00:06:28,030 --> 00:06:30,360
how heartbroken would those who admire it be?

42
00:06:36,159 --> 00:06:38,050
When the moon sets,

43
00:06:39,530 --> 00:06:40,970
the sun rises.

44
00:06:42,540 --> 00:06:44,520
Its brilliant light

45
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:46,540
outshines the moon.

46
00:06:51,030 --> 00:06:53,150
The sun blazes with scorching heat.

47
00:06:55,350 --> 00:06:57,680
Anyone who gets too close may get burned.

48
00:07:05,270 --> 00:07:07,710
Unlike the moon, whose light is gentle.

49
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:15,800
If my wish could come true,

50
00:07:17,870 --> 00:07:20,240
I’d hold on to the moon and never let it go.

51
00:07:23,230 --> 00:07:24,270
Then,

52
00:07:26,250 --> 00:07:27,610
if someone longs for something

53
00:07:29,230 --> 00:07:30,970
they can never have,

54
00:07:33,930 --> 00:07:36,070
should they keep hoping?

55
00:07:38,370 --> 00:07:40,510
Desire comes from the heart.

56
00:07:42,210 --> 00:07:44,380
You can’t force a heart to stop longing.

57
00:07:48,440 --> 00:07:52,090
Unless you know for certain that it’s impossible.

58
00:07:55,520 --> 00:07:58,560
The sooner you let go,

59
00:08:00,600 --> 00:08:02,020
the less it’ll hurt.

60
00:08:15,920 --> 00:08:17,400
I’m going back to my room.

61
00:08:55,510 --> 00:08:56,430
Gaew.

62
00:08:57,160 --> 00:08:57,900
Yes?

63
00:08:58,690 --> 00:09:00,020
Come sit with me.

64
00:09:19,790 --> 00:09:20,830
Just now,

65
00:09:21,560 --> 00:09:23,400
what were you talking about?

66
00:09:27,080 --> 00:09:28,290
Just random things

67
00:09:30,120 --> 00:09:31,030
like love.

68
00:09:34,400 --> 00:09:35,950
Is P’Sri in love?

69
00:09:39,270 --> 00:09:40,100
That’s right.

70
00:09:41,640 --> 00:09:42,360
With who?

71
00:09:48,590 --> 00:09:49,470
I don’t know.

72
00:09:56,750 --> 00:09:57,630
Do you...

73
00:09:58,820 --> 00:10:00,250
have someone in your heart?

74
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:12,270
I’m asking you.

75
00:10:13,250 --> 00:10:14,850
Do you like someone?

76
00:10:21,470 --> 00:10:22,860
Why do you want to know?

77
00:10:25,370 --> 00:10:26,800
I asked first,

78
00:10:27,780 --> 00:10:29,250
so you should answer first.

79
00:10:35,690 --> 00:10:36,960
I guess I do.

80
00:10:43,210 --> 00:10:44,560
I answered your question.

81
00:10:47,740 --> 00:10:48,980
Now it’s your turn.

82
00:10:49,970 --> 00:10:51,130
Why do you want to know?

83
00:10:56,490 --> 00:10:57,880
Love is such a curious thing.

84
00:11:00,580 --> 00:11:01,750
Even when you shouldn’t,

85
00:11:03,580 --> 00:11:05,060
it’s so hard to stop yourself.

86
00:11:12,420 --> 00:11:14,310
That doesn’t answer my question.

87
00:11:16,120 --> 00:11:18,010
You’ve fallen for someone, haven’t you?

88
00:11:24,660 --> 00:11:25,570
At first,

89
00:11:26,580 --> 00:11:28,160
I wasn’t sure.

90
00:11:31,220 --> 00:11:32,250
But now,

91
00:11:34,260 --> 00:11:35,560
I’m certain.

92
00:11:46,170 --> 00:11:47,320
Is it someone I’ve met before?

93
00:11:48,330 --> 00:11:49,400
What do they look like?

94
00:11:50,270 --> 00:11:51,150
Can you tell me?

95
00:11:55,870 --> 00:11:57,150
Do you really want to know?

96
00:11:58,560 --> 00:11:59,510
Yes.

97
00:12:06,460 --> 00:12:07,450
Then…

98
00:12:08,470 --> 00:12:10,850
go look into a looking glass,

99
00:12:11,670 --> 00:12:13,130
and you shall find the answer.

100
00:12:37,610 --> 00:12:38,800
A looking glass?

101
00:12:41,580 --> 00:12:42,950
What’s that?

102
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:47,730
A mirror?

103
00:12:55,190 --> 00:12:56,320
P'Muen.

104
00:13:23,270 --> 00:13:25,540
I’m done, my lord.

105
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:35,180
Nothing in this world compares to loving you.

106
00:13:37,420 --> 00:13:41,250
I can’t stay by your side,

107
00:13:42,790 --> 00:13:46,720
despite loving you with all my heart,

108
00:13:47,830 --> 00:13:50,410
You’re not me.

109
00:13:51,040 --> 00:13:53,290
You’ll never know how deeply this hurts.

110
00:14:02,660 --> 00:14:04,730
To love someone, but can’t be with them.

111
00:14:05,630 --> 00:14:07,560
A love that burns your heart to ashes.

112
00:14:08,940 --> 00:14:10,140
Is that right?

113
00:14:13,850 --> 00:14:14,810
Yes, my lord.

114
00:14:24,470 --> 00:14:25,360
Your turn.

115
00:14:30,850 --> 00:14:31,670
Understood.

116
00:14:36,910 --> 00:14:41,280
O moon, my heart’s true desire.

117
00:14:44,520 --> 00:14:48,570
Your radiant light is forever engraved in my heart.

118
00:14:50,170 --> 00:14:55,030
Your gentle voice has captured my soul.

119
00:14:57,380 --> 00:15:00,260
Yet you remain beyond my reach.

120
00:15:00,880 --> 00:15:03,580
O, how I long to call you mine.

121
00:15:13,640 --> 00:15:14,980
What’s gotten into you two?

122
00:15:16,170 --> 00:15:17,770
One’s heart is burning with love,

123
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:20,070
while the other’s hiding it deeply.

124
00:15:23,710 --> 00:15:25,380
Maybe Lord Sriprach

125
00:15:25,670 --> 00:15:29,550
has fallen for someone who’s already taken.

126
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:31,470
That's what i think.

127
00:15:34,930 --> 00:15:35,760
Your turn,

128
00:15:36,650 --> 00:15:37,920
Consort Thao-Srichulaluck.

129
00:15:50,400 --> 00:15:51,470
To love you,

130
00:15:52,770 --> 00:15:55,540
my heart yearns to see you.

131
00:15:58,050 --> 00:16:02,970
When we’re apart, my heart feels restless

132
00:16:05,650 --> 00:16:06,660
Perhaps this is love,

133
00:16:07,560 --> 00:16:10,740
yet fate and duty

134
00:16:12,550 --> 00:16:15,990
leave me no choice.

135
00:16:17,210 --> 00:16:19,900
Better hide it than be destroyed.

136
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:33,960
What does your poem mean?

137
00:16:40,760 --> 00:16:44,150
Duty comes before everything else.

138
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:50,570
So,

139
00:16:51,310 --> 00:16:54,050
your poem means

140
00:16:54,910 --> 00:16:58,230
that you can’t control love,

141
00:16:58,940 --> 00:17:01,820
but duty outweighs everything,

142
00:17:02,260 --> 00:17:04,660
so you can’t follow your feelings.

143
00:17:04,660 --> 00:17:05,510
Am I right?

144
00:17:11,920 --> 00:17:13,780
Three poems. Three hearts.

145
00:17:14,470 --> 00:17:16,609
Yet somehow, they seem like one story.

146
00:17:18,950 --> 00:17:19,720
Listen.

147
00:17:21,400 --> 00:17:22,690
Love isn’t wrong.

148
00:17:23,579 --> 00:17:25,079
But if you choose to love,

149
00:17:25,730 --> 00:17:26,880
choose carefully.

150
00:17:27,670 --> 00:17:29,380
So you won’t have to hide it

151
00:17:30,330 --> 00:17:33,570
or let it burn you alive.

152
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:18,790
Wad.

153
00:18:26,100 --> 00:18:27,610
What are you doing here, Reung?

154
00:18:30,870 --> 00:18:32,790
I wanted to try cockfighting,

155
00:18:33,500 --> 00:18:34,250
so I came.

156
00:18:35,290 --> 00:18:37,070
Are you sure?

157
00:18:37,870 --> 00:18:38,900
Of course.

158
00:18:40,070 --> 00:18:40,680
Why?

159
00:18:41,430 --> 00:18:43,310
Do you really not know?

160
00:18:43,960 --> 00:18:46,060
The one you brought is a hen.

161
00:18:52,340 --> 00:18:53,300
Oh.

162
00:18:54,590 --> 00:18:55,460
I just–

163
00:18:55,460 --> 00:18:56,760
Spare me the excuse.

164
00:18:57,700 --> 00:19:00,470
Everyone knows you hate loud noises.

165
00:19:02,380 --> 00:19:05,090
No one’s buying your excuse.

166
00:19:06,200 --> 00:19:07,650
Just tell the truth.

167
00:19:08,010 --> 00:19:09,870
Why are you really here?

168
00:19:11,920 --> 00:19:14,010
Well, I…

169
00:19:14,010 --> 00:19:14,720
Wad.

170
00:19:24,040 --> 00:19:24,710
Wad.

171
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:28,560
Whether you meant to or not,

172
00:19:29,530 --> 00:19:31,300
I want you to think it over.

173
00:19:32,210 --> 00:19:33,970
We’re friends anyway.

174
00:19:40,100 --> 00:19:41,460
Do what you have to do.

175
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:51,800
Dech, you’re better now?

176
00:19:53,090 --> 00:19:53,990
Yeah, I’m all good.

177
00:19:57,260 --> 00:19:58,610
-How did you—
-Dech.

178
00:19:59,490 --> 00:20:01,000
Come check out my new chicken.

179
00:20:02,410 --> 00:20:02,990
Sure.

180
00:20:07,660 --> 00:20:08,390
Gaew.

181
00:20:10,020 --> 00:20:11,520
I’m sorry

182
00:20:12,790 --> 00:20:15,840
for messing with you that day,

183
00:20:16,630 --> 00:20:18,060
and causing Dech trouble.

184
00:20:19,130 --> 00:20:20,890
I’ve forgotten all about it.

185
00:20:21,580 --> 00:20:22,830
I should apologize too.

186
00:20:23,280 --> 00:20:25,450
I lost my temper that day.

187
00:20:28,120 --> 00:20:29,380
Thank you.

188
00:20:33,330 --> 00:20:34,120
Gaew.

189
00:20:35,420 --> 00:20:36,860
You invited me here,

190
00:20:36,860 --> 00:20:38,660
so why do you keep talking to Wad?

191
00:20:39,050 --> 00:20:39,860
Come here.

192
00:20:40,290 --> 00:20:40,870
Yes.

193
00:20:41,130 --> 00:20:42,840
Let’s get started.

194
00:20:49,320 --> 00:20:51,270
Go, Thongkam!

195
00:20:53,050 --> 00:20:55,760
Night Fury, don’t lose.

196
00:20:56,030 --> 00:20:57,160
Okay?

197
00:20:57,160 --> 00:20:58,670
Do you want to use my hen?

198
00:20:58,670 --> 00:21:00,600
No, save it for laying eggs.

199
00:21:02,220 --> 00:21:03,170
Go!

200
00:21:14,790 --> 00:21:15,500
Come on!

201
00:21:15,930 --> 00:21:17,260
That’s it, Thongkam!

202
00:21:20,450 --> 00:21:21,430
Good job!

203
00:21:22,260 --> 00:21:23,290
Your rooster’s good.

204
00:21:27,760 --> 00:21:28,950
Thanks, Reung.

205
00:21:33,240 --> 00:21:34,680
Well done, Wad.

206
00:21:55,830 --> 00:21:56,930
Today is a good day.

207
00:21:57,830 --> 00:21:59,960
All my friends are together.

208
00:22:00,890 --> 00:22:01,980
I’m really happy.

209
00:22:04,620 --> 00:22:06,010
Drink up.

210
00:22:07,130 --> 00:22:07,850
Cheers.

211
00:22:16,060 --> 00:22:19,000
It’s been a long time since we drank together.

212
00:22:24,850 --> 00:22:25,750
Guys,

213
00:22:26,430 --> 00:22:27,630
want to play a game?

214
00:22:28,490 --> 00:22:29,540
What’s a game?

215
00:22:31,840 --> 00:22:33,630
A game is a pastime.

216
00:22:34,740 --> 00:22:37,060
This one’s called

217
00:22:37,500 --> 00:22:38,780
“Yes or No.”

218
00:22:40,390 --> 00:22:42,680
I’ll spin P’Dech’s dagger.

219
00:22:43,160 --> 00:22:45,630
Whoever it points to

220
00:22:46,030 --> 00:22:49,290
has to answer a question with…

221
00:22:49,290 --> 00:22:50,330
“Yes.” or “No.”

222
00:22:51,750 --> 00:22:55,190
If it’s yes, you say, “Yes, of course.”

223
00:22:56,310 --> 00:22:58,960
If it’s no, or you don’t want to answer,

224
00:22:59,550 --> 00:23:01,200
you lose.

225
00:23:01,650 --> 00:23:02,960
Then you have to take a shot.

226
00:23:05,520 --> 00:23:06,560
Let’s play.

227
00:23:11,880 --> 00:23:12,830
P’Muen.

228
00:23:14,110 --> 00:23:14,820
Me?

229
00:23:14,820 --> 00:23:15,860
Here’s your question.

230
00:23:16,770 --> 00:23:20,490
Do you like sneaking glances at me?

231
00:23:25,310 --> 00:23:25,990
Dech.

232
00:23:33,640 --> 00:23:34,560
Yes, of course.

233
00:23:34,560 --> 00:23:36,090
Hm?

234
00:23:38,370 --> 00:23:39,990
But I only keep an eye on you

235
00:23:40,900 --> 00:23:43,190
because I’m worried you’ll go fooling around.

236
00:23:43,950 --> 00:23:44,700
That’s all.

237
00:23:50,640 --> 00:23:51,940
You’re acting all cool.

238
00:23:55,630 --> 00:23:56,560
Reung.

239
00:24:02,850 --> 00:24:03,550
Come on.

240
00:24:04,310 --> 00:24:05,240
Round two.

241
00:24:09,700 --> 00:24:10,700
P’Muen again.

242
00:24:11,270 --> 00:24:12,360
Me again?

243
00:24:12,990 --> 00:24:14,120
The question is…

244
00:24:14,650 --> 00:24:19,140
Do you enjoy being alone with me?

245
00:24:19,560 --> 00:24:20,490
Yes or no?

246
00:24:27,010 --> 00:24:27,970
Uh…

247
00:24:28,790 --> 00:24:29,820
Yes, of course.

248
00:24:31,310 --> 00:24:34,150
I always see him smiling from ear to ear

249
00:24:34,150 --> 00:24:36,930
whenever he’s alone with you.

250
00:24:37,410 --> 00:24:39,460
Pin, shut up!

251
00:24:40,090 --> 00:24:41,120
Sorry, my lord.

252
00:24:41,390 --> 00:24:42,270
You little…

253
00:24:43,720 --> 00:24:44,490
Damn.

254
00:24:46,580 --> 00:24:47,260
Alright.

255
00:24:48,120 --> 00:24:48,990
Round three.

256
00:24:54,040 --> 00:24:54,750
Oh!

257
00:24:55,750 --> 00:24:56,540
P'Muen!

258
00:24:56,770 --> 00:24:57,390
Huh?

259
00:24:58,060 --> 00:25:00,130
Why does it keep pointing at me?

260
00:25:01,340 --> 00:25:02,520
Are you messing with me?

261
00:25:03,360 --> 00:25:04,410
I’m not.

262
00:25:05,140 --> 00:25:05,690
Alright.

263
00:25:06,950 --> 00:25:08,690
I’ll ask the last question.

264
00:25:13,490 --> 00:25:15,180
If I disappeared from here,

265
00:25:15,980 --> 00:25:17,320
would you miss me?

266
00:25:17,870 --> 00:25:18,670
Yes or no?

267
00:25:32,940 --> 00:25:33,700
I'll miss you.

268
00:25:41,010 --> 00:25:42,590
Is that so, Dech?

269
00:25:47,400 --> 00:25:49,070
If any of my friends here

270
00:25:49,800 --> 00:25:51,180
were to disappear,

271
00:25:52,060 --> 00:25:53,090
I’d miss every one of them.

272
00:25:53,780 --> 00:25:54,910
Is that so?

273
00:25:58,400 --> 00:25:59,300
That’s right.

274
00:26:02,070 --> 00:26:02,780
Wad.

275
00:26:04,180 --> 00:26:05,820
Do you want to play this game with Reung?

276
00:26:12,790 --> 00:26:13,590
-No.
-No.

277
00:26:19,750 --> 00:26:20,860
-I do.
-I do.

278
00:26:21,910 --> 00:26:23,170
I want to play with Yam.

279
00:26:24,670 --> 00:26:25,750
Who wants to play with you?

280
00:26:26,500 --> 00:26:28,030
Come on, Yam.

281
00:26:28,810 --> 00:26:30,190
It’s just for fun.

282
00:26:31,570 --> 00:26:32,220
Then

283
00:26:32,910 --> 00:26:34,190
you don’t have to spin the dagger,

284
00:26:34,980 --> 00:26:36,230
just take turns asking.

285
00:26:36,950 --> 00:26:37,980
Then I’ll go first.

286
00:26:39,310 --> 00:26:40,050
Yam.

287
00:26:40,800 --> 00:26:44,040
Do you like peeping at me while I bathe? Yes or no?

288
00:26:44,250 --> 00:26:45,260
Yes, of course.

289
00:26:45,900 --> 00:26:46,790
Huh?

290
00:26:47,450 --> 00:26:48,810
I knew it!

291
00:26:49,330 --> 00:26:52,260
I only keep an eye on you to make sure

292
00:26:52,930 --> 00:26:56,120
you don’t go fooling around.

293
00:27:00,640 --> 00:27:03,510
If I disappeared one day,

294
00:27:04,010 --> 00:27:06,660
would anyone miss me?

295
00:27:11,480 --> 00:27:12,540
I don’t get it.

296
00:27:13,380 --> 00:27:15,240
You lost. Drink.

297
00:27:15,510 --> 00:27:16,480
Have a drink with me.

298
00:27:16,920 --> 00:27:18,360
-Drink it yourself.
Come on.

299
00:27:19,800 --> 00:27:21,060
Let's drink together.

300
00:27:21,440 --> 00:27:22,980
Yeah?

301
00:27:22,980 --> 00:27:23,890
Cheers.

302
00:27:42,510 --> 00:27:43,470
Go for it!

303
00:27:54,480 --> 00:27:55,370
That’s it.

304
00:28:03,510 --> 00:28:05,390
Yeah,

305
00:28:05,390 --> 00:28:07,260
don’t back down.

306
00:28:07,260 --> 00:28:09,160
That’s the spirit.

307
00:28:11,050 --> 00:28:11,720
Yam.

308
00:28:12,550 --> 00:28:15,780
Do you like peeping at me while I bathe? Yes or no?

309
00:28:16,000 --> 00:28:17,070
Yes, of course.

310
00:28:17,790 --> 00:28:19,190
I knew it!

311
00:28:41,750 --> 00:28:42,850
What am I staring at?

312
00:28:43,880 --> 00:28:45,200
Stop thinking. Stop looking.

313
00:28:45,850 --> 00:28:46,590
Stop.

314
00:28:47,420 --> 00:28:48,530
Just stop.

315
00:29:01,870 --> 00:29:02,920
Come on, you can do it.

316
00:29:05,070 --> 00:29:06,550
You’re almost there.

317
00:29:10,300 --> 00:29:11,900
That’s it!

318
00:29:12,800 --> 00:29:13,510
Go.

319
00:29:24,540 --> 00:29:26,540
You can do it.

320
00:29:31,950 --> 00:29:33,170
Restrain the heart.

321
00:29:34,020 --> 00:29:35,170
Don’t let your heart waver.

322
00:29:35,170 --> 00:29:36,640
Don't let your mind wander afar.

323
00:29:37,470 --> 00:29:38,630
Restrain the heart.

324
00:29:39,230 --> 00:29:40,360
Don’t let your heart waver.

325
00:29:40,970 --> 00:29:42,400
Don't let your mind wander afar.

326
00:29:45,700 --> 00:29:46,410
Ah!

327
00:29:48,220 --> 00:29:49,240
It's nothing.

328
00:29:52,240 --> 00:29:55,200
Just a little more!

329
00:30:09,750 --> 00:30:11,000
Restrain the heart.

330
00:30:11,470 --> 00:30:12,500
Don’t let your heart waver.

331
00:30:12,920 --> 00:30:14,380
Don't let your mind wander afar.

332
00:30:16,160 --> 00:30:17,390
Restrain the heart.

333
00:30:17,590 --> 00:30:18,580
Don’t let your heart waver.

334
00:30:19,110 --> 00:30:20,410
Don't let your mind wander afar.

335
00:30:25,660 --> 00:30:26,930
Restrain the heart.

336
00:30:27,350 --> 00:30:28,420
Don’t let your heart waver.

337
00:30:28,850 --> 00:30:30,220
Don't let your mind wander afar.

338
00:30:35,590 --> 00:30:36,330
Ah!

339
00:30:36,980 --> 00:30:37,870
What are you doing?

340
00:30:39,820 --> 00:30:40,840
Nothing.

341
00:30:42,720 --> 00:30:44,150
But I saw you chanting something.

342
00:30:45,160 --> 00:30:46,060
What chant was that?

343
00:30:49,010 --> 00:30:50,390
It’s a heart restraining spell

344
00:30:52,900 --> 00:30:54,080
Restrain the heart.

345
00:30:54,370 --> 00:30:55,470
Don’t let your heart waver.

346
00:30:55,900 --> 00:30:57,220
Don't let your mind wander afar.

347
00:30:59,750 --> 00:31:00,700
What do you use it for?

348
00:31:02,470 --> 00:31:05,040
To stop myself from loving someone.

349
00:31:09,370 --> 00:31:10,390
Who are you in love with?

350
00:31:11,260 --> 00:31:12,890
Uh…

351
00:31:14,000 --> 00:31:14,890
No one.

352
00:31:21,160 --> 00:31:22,630
Restrain the heart.

353
00:31:23,090 --> 00:31:24,470
Don’t let your heart waver.

354
00:31:25,310 --> 00:31:26,950
Don't let your mind wander afar.

355
00:31:28,140 --> 00:31:29,100
P’Muen.

356
00:31:34,140 --> 00:31:35,260
-Uh…
-P’Muen.

357
00:31:35,860 --> 00:31:36,810
Hold on, P’Muen.

358
00:31:39,040 --> 00:31:40,890
Restrain the heart.

359
00:31:40,890 --> 00:31:42,200
Don’t let your heart waver.

360
00:31:42,480 --> 00:31:44,180
Don't let your mind wander afar.

361
00:31:45,940 --> 00:31:47,150
What are you chanting?

362
00:32:01,870 --> 00:32:03,060
I’m not chanting anything.

363
00:32:05,280 --> 00:32:06,160
Are you sure?

364
00:32:10,760 --> 00:32:11,850
What kind of spell is it?

365
00:32:14,330 --> 00:32:17,030
Don’t come any closer.

366
00:32:17,910 --> 00:32:19,360
It’s just a mosquito repelling spell.

367
00:32:20,930 --> 00:32:21,710
Huh?

368
00:32:22,370 --> 00:32:23,310
Mosquito Repellent?

369
00:32:28,800 --> 00:32:29,890
Restrain the heart.

370
00:32:30,140 --> 00:32:31,380
Don’t let your heart waver.

371
00:32:31,600 --> 00:32:32,970
Don't let your mind wander afar.

372
00:32:39,300 --> 00:32:41,410
Don't let your mind wander afar?

373
00:32:43,810 --> 00:32:47,190
But my heart has already wandered far, P’Muen.

374
00:33:16,830 --> 00:33:18,050
Restrain the heart.

375
00:33:18,600 --> 00:33:19,830
Don’t let your heart waver.

376
00:33:20,180 --> 00:33:21,680
Don't let your mind wander afar.

377
00:33:22,690 --> 00:33:23,990
Restrain the heart.

378
00:33:24,240 --> 00:33:25,410
Don’t let your heart waver.

379
00:33:25,750 --> 00:33:27,290
Don't let your mind wander afar.

380
00:33:33,570 --> 00:33:34,710
What are you staring at?

381
00:33:34,710 --> 00:33:35,830
What’s wrong with you?

382
00:33:36,860 --> 00:33:37,880
Nothing.

383
00:33:40,110 --> 00:33:41,550
You’re so dead tonight.

384
00:33:41,920 --> 00:33:43,230
You think I’m scared?

385
00:33:53,770 --> 00:33:54,700
I can’t hold it in anymore.

386
00:33:54,700 --> 00:33:55,820
Hold what?

387
00:34:02,030 --> 00:34:03,480
What the hell, Pin?

388
00:34:06,510 --> 00:34:07,530
I can’t hold it in anymore.

389
00:34:08,120 --> 00:34:09,340
I’m leaving.

390
00:34:09,659 --> 00:34:10,400
What an ass!

391
00:34:14,650 --> 00:34:15,690
Where are you going?

392
00:34:16,690 --> 00:34:17,449
Yam.

393
00:34:18,250 --> 00:34:19,429
Can you sleep with me tonight?

394
00:34:32,730 --> 00:34:34,440
Why do you want me to sleep with you?

395
00:34:37,330 --> 00:34:38,139
I just asked.

396
00:34:40,770 --> 00:34:41,820
So why did you come?

397
00:35:03,600 --> 00:35:05,220
I can’t hold it in anymore either.

398
00:35:16,680 --> 00:35:17,460
P’Muen!

399
00:35:18,430 --> 00:35:19,170
P’Muen.

400
00:35:25,350 --> 00:35:26,400
Where are you going?

401
00:35:26,740 --> 00:35:28,990
I saw Pin packing your things this morning.

402
00:35:30,270 --> 00:35:32,320
I have business in Lavo.

403
00:35:32,750 --> 00:35:34,090
Lavo?

404
00:35:35,230 --> 00:35:36,110
Lopburi Province?

405
00:35:36,970 --> 00:35:37,450
Mhm.

406
00:35:37,680 --> 00:35:38,680
Can I come with you?

407
00:35:40,050 --> 00:35:41,670
I want to see Lavo with my own eyes,

408
00:35:42,090 --> 00:35:43,200
and go sightseeing.

409
00:35:45,770 --> 00:35:46,460
No.

410
00:35:46,970 --> 00:35:48,620
I’m going to work, not to travel.

411
00:35:49,530 --> 00:35:51,050
Just finish your work first,

412
00:35:51,050 --> 00:35:54,280
then take me sightseeing after that.

413
00:35:58,520 --> 00:35:59,760
Does Lavo have any waterfalls?

414
00:36:01,220 --> 00:36:02,150
Yeah.

415
00:36:03,050 --> 00:36:03,840
Then I’m coming too.

416
00:36:05,720 --> 00:36:07,060
I promise I’ll be good.

417
00:36:08,710 --> 00:36:10,140
Deal. Then I’ll go change first.

418
00:36:10,890 --> 00:36:11,710
Gaew.

419
00:36:12,300 --> 00:36:13,110
Gaew!

420
00:36:16,570 --> 00:36:17,480
What does “deal” mean?

421
00:36:37,350 --> 00:36:38,110
Gaew?

422
00:36:40,880 --> 00:36:41,650
Gaew!

423
00:36:44,200 --> 00:36:45,020
Gaew!

424
00:36:45,540 --> 00:36:46,320
Gaew!

425
00:36:52,320 --> 00:36:54,830
What are you doing? You scared me to death.

426
00:36:55,400 --> 00:36:56,980
Were you afraid I’d drown?

427
00:36:58,420 --> 00:36:59,760
Don’t ever do that again.

428
00:37:03,220 --> 00:37:04,740
I just wanted to see

429
00:37:04,740 --> 00:37:06,210
if I fell into the water again,

430
00:37:06,530 --> 00:37:08,120
would you save me?

431
00:37:09,100 --> 00:37:11,300
You know I can’t swim.

432
00:37:12,650 --> 00:37:14,530
Come on, I’ll teach you.

433
00:37:36,620 --> 00:37:39,080
Don’t be scared. The water’s shallow.

434
00:37:45,940 --> 00:37:47,070
Hey, Gaew!

435
00:38:11,030 --> 00:38:11,920
P’Muen.

436
00:38:12,070 --> 00:38:12,690
Huh?

437
00:38:13,330 --> 00:38:14,350
Can I ask you something?

438
00:38:14,940 --> 00:38:15,650
Sure.

439
00:38:17,560 --> 00:38:19,240
You like me, don’t you?

440
00:38:23,050 --> 00:38:24,140
What kind of question is that?

441
00:38:27,990 --> 00:38:29,170
Yes or no?

442
00:38:33,730 --> 00:38:35,360
I’m being honest with you.

443
00:38:36,200 --> 00:38:38,010
Can you be honest with me too?

444
00:38:39,080 --> 00:38:41,190
Don’t make me keep guessing.

445
00:38:42,160 --> 00:38:43,070
So…

446
00:38:44,680 --> 00:38:46,320
You like me, don’t you?

447
00:38:56,830 --> 00:39:02,230
Oh, my heart has belonged to none

448
00:39:03,490 --> 00:39:08,970
No one ever walked in, not a single one

449
00:39:10,150 --> 00:39:15,990
I believe the time will come someday

450
00:39:16,990 --> 00:39:22,830
That fate will lead you to my way

451
00:39:23,220 --> 00:39:31,000
Guided by fate, our paths finally crossed

452
00:39:31,000 --> 00:39:34,630
Just one glance, and my heart starts to sway

453
00:39:34,630 --> 00:39:40,550
Don't know why I’m carried far away

454
00:39:41,470 --> 00:39:48,350
Are you the one I’ve waited for so long?

455
00:39:48,350 --> 00:39:54,990
Never has my heart yearned quite this strong

456
00:39:54,990 --> 00:40:01,760
If heaven decreed that we are meant to be

457
00:40:01,760 --> 00:40:06,970
How could I deny the feelings inside of me?

458
00:40:06,970 --> 00:40:11,370
Oh, my beloved

459
00:40:11,510 --> 00:40:12,200
P'Yam.

460
00:40:13,580 --> 00:40:14,260
P'Yam?

461
00:40:44,260 --> 00:40:48,100
I loved you before he stole you away.

462
00:40:49,650 --> 00:40:53,570
Fate has cruelly played with my heart.

463
00:40:54,250 --> 00:40:57,910
I am heartbroken and cannot pretend to be happy.

464
00:40:59,020 --> 00:41:01,490
I will never surrender.

465
00:41:02,990 --> 00:41:05,750
I will fight until my last breath.

466
00:41:20,520 --> 00:41:21,280
Gaew.

467
00:41:24,150 --> 00:41:26,630
Did you leave this poem here?

468
00:41:27,360 --> 00:41:28,230
This is so risky.

469
00:41:31,790 --> 00:41:33,040
Give it back.

470
00:41:40,040 --> 00:41:41,680
Your feelings are too obvious.

471
00:41:42,100 --> 00:41:43,540
It’s dangerous, P’Sri.

472
00:41:44,670 --> 00:41:45,760
What are you talking about?

473
00:41:48,590 --> 00:41:49,920
Can I read your fortune?

474
00:41:50,950 --> 00:41:52,720
I know a thing or two about fortune telling.

475
00:41:53,720 --> 00:41:55,300
Your fate is written all over your face.

476
00:41:56,120 --> 00:41:57,120
I think I can read it.

477
00:41:58,250 --> 00:42:00,010
Since when did you know fortune telling?

478
00:42:01,950 --> 00:42:02,720
P’Sri.

479
00:42:05,100 --> 00:42:06,100
You‘re destined

480
00:42:07,350 --> 00:42:08,670
to rise in rank.

481
00:42:10,640 --> 00:42:12,270
Politics won’t be your downfall,

482
00:42:16,810 --> 00:42:18,130
but love will.

483
00:42:22,510 --> 00:42:24,610
My heart will be my downfall?

484
00:42:26,020 --> 00:42:27,090
I’m not joking.

485
00:42:28,690 --> 00:42:29,720
With a fate like yours,

486
00:42:31,180 --> 00:42:33,040
if you keep going down this path,

487
00:42:34,700 --> 00:42:36,340
your heart will bring you disaster.

488
00:42:40,550 --> 00:42:42,740
At first, it’ll be a secret.

489
00:42:44,300 --> 00:42:47,030
Then, an accusation.

490
00:42:49,150 --> 00:42:50,170
And in the end,

491
00:42:50,950 --> 00:42:52,400
it’ll become a crime.

492
00:42:57,920 --> 00:42:59,930
I can see a parting.

493
00:43:03,550 --> 00:43:04,940
A goodbye…

494
00:43:05,720 --> 00:43:07,280
that can’t be spoken.

495
00:43:09,930 --> 00:43:11,970
Believe me, P'Sri.

496
00:43:14,870 --> 00:43:16,400
If you step back now,

497
00:43:17,420 --> 00:43:20,910
you might be able to save your life and honor.

498
00:43:23,880 --> 00:43:25,430
The way you talk…

499
00:43:28,030 --> 00:43:30,490
doesn’t sound like an ordinary fortune teller.

500
00:43:33,150 --> 00:43:35,400
I’m only telling you what I see.

501
00:43:36,820 --> 00:43:38,050
If you don’t believe me,

502
00:43:39,410 --> 00:43:40,480
it’s up to you.

503
00:43:41,980 --> 00:43:43,990
You didn’t just tell me what would happen.

504
00:43:45,230 --> 00:43:46,990
You even told me how it would unfold.

505
00:43:49,420 --> 00:43:50,580
From a secret,

506
00:43:51,330 --> 00:43:52,500
to an accusation,

507
00:43:53,990 --> 00:43:55,010
to a crime.

508
00:43:56,470 --> 00:43:58,220
This isn’t a guess. You already know.

509
00:44:05,020 --> 00:44:05,830
Some things…

510
00:44:07,050 --> 00:44:08,500
once you’ve seen them happen,

511
00:44:09,990 --> 00:44:11,320
you already know how they’ll end.

512
00:44:13,090 --> 00:44:14,560
You’ve seen it before?

513
00:44:16,800 --> 00:44:17,850
What do you mean?

514
00:44:18,600 --> 00:44:20,850
Where did you see it?

515
00:44:28,140 --> 00:44:30,560
Why do you know my fate,

516
00:44:31,320 --> 00:44:33,140
as if you’ve already lived through it?

517
00:44:34,790 --> 00:44:37,970
Why do you know how it’ll turn out?

518
00:44:39,500 --> 00:44:41,680
And why are you telling me to turn back,

519
00:44:42,610 --> 00:44:44,590
as if you’ve already seen me fall?

520
00:44:47,400 --> 00:44:49,770
I just don’t want you to get hurt, P’Sri.

521
00:44:49,770 --> 00:44:51,070
Don't avoid my question.

522
00:44:54,210 --> 00:44:55,980
Who exactly are you?

523
00:45:02,850 --> 00:45:03,790
I’m…

524
00:45:04,530 --> 00:45:05,320
Gaew.

525
00:45:06,450 --> 00:45:08,000
Your younger brother.

526
00:45:10,420 --> 00:45:11,140
No.

527
00:45:14,090 --> 00:45:17,230
Gaew doesn’t know other people’s fate.

528
00:45:19,130 --> 00:45:22,990
And he wouldn’t talk about parting as if he’s lived through it.

529
00:45:25,880 --> 00:45:28,470
If you’re bold enough to talk about my life,

530
00:45:29,180 --> 00:45:30,900
then you should be able to tell me.

531
00:45:32,730 --> 00:45:34,430
Where did you come from?

532
00:45:37,590 --> 00:45:38,680
Answer me.

533
00:45:41,350 --> 00:45:43,710
Are you really Gaew?

534
00:45:46,040 --> 00:45:47,710
Or someone else?

535
00:45:48,800 --> 00:45:50,170
Who are you, really?

536
00:46:32,870 --> 00:46:34,010
Are you feeling unwell?

537
00:46:34,010 --> 00:46:37,070
Will this really make me feel better, P’Muen?

538
00:46:37,780 --> 00:46:38,560
Trust me.

539
00:46:39,100 --> 00:46:39,840
Reung.

540
00:46:40,820 --> 00:46:42,430
Do you like me?

541
00:46:43,600 --> 00:46:45,030
If I get to stay here,

542
00:46:45,450 --> 00:46:47,900
I’ll celebrate Loy Krathong with you every year.

543
00:46:48,470 --> 00:46:49,250
Confirm.

544
00:46:53,140 --> 00:46:54,330
How could you do this?

545
00:46:54,330 --> 00:46:57,020
You should never tell our family’s business to outsiders!

546
00:47:19,530 --> 00:47:20,220
P’Khun.

547
00:47:22,870 --> 00:47:23,680
P’Khun.
